# factlattice-reviewer: shipped configuration [SPEC:REVIEWER-CONFIG-DOC]

This file ships with the engine and holds NO site values. A site's values live in ONE node, REVIEWER-SITE-CONFIG, in a registered corpus outside the engine repository, so that an engine go-live can never overwrite them. The reviewer finds it with a corpus-omitted lts_find on the prefix REVIEWER-SITE-CONFIG: exactly one must exist. Zero means no site configuration; two or more stops the run with no-output-root, naming both. The shipped node and the site node use the same three keys.

The value `none` means unset. The three keys are declared in the reviewer profile, and a test pins them.

## [REVIEWER-CONFIG] Shipped reviewer configuration (no site values)

- default-output-root: none
- corpus-output-overrides: none
- default-root-corpora: none

default-output-root is the folder reviews go to for corpora on default-root-corpora. corpus-output-overrides is a list of items of the form `<corpus-id>[:<path-prefix>] -> <folder>`; the longest matching prefix wins and an override beats a profile review-output, which beats the default. default-root-corpora lists the corpora the default folder applies to; a corpus the engine treats as private never uses the default folder, even if it is listed.
